// assets/media/veo_budget.ron
// The total-spend budget for paid Veo generations and image-model requests, read by
// `asset_baker generate-veo` and `asset_baker effect-image`.
//
// Not a secret. The owner's rule (chat, 2026-11-05, recorded in
// docs/questions/closed/0024-veo-billing-and-weekly-cap.md and the Veo plan's D-12): "the only
// bro limit you need to take into account are the 200$. no weekly, round or batch limit (unless
// it's a limit dictated by Google)". There is no per-run or rolling-window cap; Google's quota refusals
// stop a run, and the next run resumes.
//
// - `total_budget_usd_cents`: the most every generation the service accepted may cost together,
//   at list price, in US cents. Spend is summed from the ledger's `request_started` lines (a
//   start the service refused for quota costs nothing); a run is charged its whole
//   `--max-generations` before it starts. $200.00 is below the owner's 200 EUR allowance.
// - `price_per_generation_usd_cents`: the list price of one generation, in US cents, per model
//   id. A ledger line or a run whose model is missing here is refused, never counted as free.
//   `veo-3.1-fast-generate-001`: one 4 s 720p clip with sound at $0.10 a second (the rate the
//   batch evidence in docs/evidence/veo/ uses).
//   Image models (effect textures, plan docs/plans/2026-11-09-effect-visualization.md §6.6 and
//   Q0078): one generated or edited image, budgeted at the dearer model's 2K price of $0.101,
//   rounded up to 11 cents, for every image model id (the plan's rule "budgeted at the higher
//   price"). `asset_baker effect-image` refuses a model id that has no price here.
(
    total_budget_usd_cents: 20000,
    price_per_generation_usd_cents: {
        "veo-3.1-fast-generate-001": 40,
        "gemini-nano-banana-2.1": 11,
        "gemini-3.1-flash-image": 11,
    },
)
